# Oscar (Brown CCV): hierarchical, spack-built Lmod. The MPI module must be loaded
# first; the *-mpi libraries built against it only appear afterwards.
# Seen on Oscar 2026-11-09 (by a CCV user, after `module purge`; C-Star runs
# `module reset`): these three load in this order and pull in hdf5-mpi/1.14.6,
# netcdf-c-mpi/4.9.3 and netcdf-fortran-mpi/4.6.1 as dependencies. Version-only
# names resolve to the site's spack-hashed module names (hpcx-mpi/2.25.1s loads
# hpcx-mpi/2.25.1s-le4f).
hpcx-mpi/2.25.1s  # site-recommended MPI (SLURM/PMIx integrated); its mpifort wraps the system gfortran 11.5
# The netcdf-mpi bundle loads netCDF-C and netCDF-Fortran and sets NETCDF, which
# oscar.env uses for both prefixes. Oscar has two netcdf-c-mpi/4.9.3 builds, and
# the default is not the one the bundle loads alongside netcdf-fortran-mpi, so
# load the bundle rather than naming the two libraries.
netcdf-mpi/4.9.3
parallel-netcdf-mpi/1.14.0  # for ParallelIO
